<% content_for :title, "Founder Letter | Hampton Lab" %>
<% content_for :description, "Why Waseem Mehany started Hampton Lab: websites built by good people, with upfront pricing, clear timelines, and nothing you don't need." %>
<% content_for :canonical_path, "/founder_letter/" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
<%= json_ld_tag({
  "@context" => "https://schema.org",
  "@graph" => [
    {
      "@type" => "AboutPage",
      "@id" => site_url("/founder_letter/"),
      "url" => site_url("/founder_letter/"),
      "name" => "A company forged out of frustration.",
      "inLanguage" => "en",
      "isPartOf" => { "@id" => site_url("/#website") },
      "about" => { "@id" => site_url("/#organization") },
      "author" => { "@id" => site_url("/founder_letter/#founder") }
    }
  ]
}) %>
<% end %>
<%= render "header/nav" %>

<main class="bg-beige">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <h1 class="text-center">A company <i>forged</i> out of frustration.</h1>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <!-- Stacked paper effect -->
  <section class="letters">
    <div class="letter__container">
      <div class="letters__main">
        <div class="letters__paragraph">
          <h3>
            You need a website. The agencies want to sell you everything else.
            <br>
            I tried hiring one last year. Twelve-page proposals. Strategy sessions. Brand audits. Social media packages. All I wanted was a clean site that worked.
          </h3>
        </div>
        <div class="letters__paragraph">
          <h3>
            The DIY route isn't better.
            <br>
            WordPress, Squarespace, Wix—each promises simplicity. Each delivers complexity. You spend weekends wrestling with plugins instead of running your business. Your site ends up looking like everyone else's. Generic templates. No character.
          </h3>
        </div>
        <div class="letters__paragraph">
          <h3>
            Here's what I learned:
            <br>
            Good websites need good people, not fancy platforms. Not AI. Not offshore teams working for pennies.
          </h3>
        </div>
        <div class="letters__paragraph">
          <h3>You wouldn't fix your own plumbing. You wouldn't perform your own surgery. Why build your own website?</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="letters__paragraph">
          <h3>
            So I started <strong>Hampton Lab</strong>.
            <br>
            We build websites. Nothing more, nothing less. You'll know the price upfront. You'll know when it's done. You'll know exactly what you're getting.
            <br>
            We work with people who value craft over complications. If that's you, let's talk.
          </h3>
        </div>
        <div class="letters__paragraph">
          <%= image_tag("signature.jpg", alt: "Waseem Mehany's signature", loading: "lazy", decoding: "async") %>
          <h3><strong>Waseem Mehany</strong></h3>
          <h3>Founder, Hampton Lab.</h3>
          <a href="mailto:waseem.mehany@hamptonlab.com"><h3>waseem.mehany@hamptonlab.com</h3></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
